country is bordered by the Red Sea, extending 1,212 kilometers from Ras Kasar in the north to Dar Elwa
in the southeast. Djibouti borders Eritrea in the southeast, Ethiopia in the south, and the Sudan in the north
and west. Administratively, the country is divided into six zobas (regions): Anseba, Debub, Debubawi Keih
Bahri, Gash-Barka, Maekel, and Semenawi Keih Bahri (see map).
Eritrea is a land of contrasts with land rising from below sea level to 3,000 meters above sea level.
There are three major physiographic zones: the Western Lowlands, the Central and Northern Highlands,
and the Eastern Lowlands (also referred to as the Coastal Plains). Temperature varies with altitude: the

